meta {
  name: tag: onlyoffice (documentserver)
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/onlyoffice/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "pod_definition": {
      "description": "ONLYOFFICE Document Server (single-container). Bundles its own postgres/redis/rabbitmq inside the image - good for a personal editor or proof of concept. For HA/scale use the onlyoffice stack tag instead.",
      "image": "onlyoffice/documentserver:latest",
      "secret_map": {
        "JWT_SECRET": "${pods:random:32}"
      },
      "environment_variables": {
        "JWT_ENABLED": "true",
        "JWT_HEADER": "Authorization",
        "JWT_SECRET": "${pods:secrets:JWT_SECRET}"
      },
      "networking": {
        "default": {
          "protocol": "http",
          "port": 80,
          "tapis_auth": true,
          "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
          "tapis_auth_return_path": "/welcome/",
          "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
          "tapis_ui_uri_description": "ONLYOFFICE Document Server - editor API + welcome page"
        }
      },
      "resources": { "cpu_request": 500, "cpu_limit": 4000, "mem_request": 1024, "mem_limit": 6144 },
      "time_to_stop_default": -1
    },
    "tag": "single",
    "commit_message": "ONLYOFFICE Document Server single-container with JWT enabled (random secret). Editor API on port 80, tapis-auth gated."
  }
}

docs {
  ## ONLYOFFICE Document Server - single container
  
  **Self-hostable: yes.** `onlyoffice/documentserver` is the open-source Document Server (Docs
  Community Edition) - the editing engine that renders/edits docx, xlsx, pptx and PDFs and that
  apps like Nextcloud/Seafile embed. This single-pod tag runs the all-in-one image, which carries
  its **own postgres, redis and rabbitmq inside the container**, so **1 container** is enough to
  get going.
  
  ### JWT is mandatory in modern builds
  The editor refuses unsigned requests by default. `JWT_ENABLED=true` + a random `JWT_SECRET` is
  set here; whatever app embeds the editor (or your API calls) must sign its config payloads with
  that same secret. Read it back from the pod's secret to configure the embedding app.
  
  ### When to move to the stack
  The bundled datastores live on the container's ephemeral disk and don't scale. For persistence
  across restarts and for multiple Document Server replicas, use
  `Create stack template tag (onlyoffice)` which externalises postgres + redis + rabbitmq.
  
  ### Instantiate
  `POST /pods` with `{ "template": "onlyoffice:single", "pod_id": "myoffice" }`
  -> editor at `myoffice.pods.<base>` (the `/welcome/` page confirms it's up).
  
  > It's an *editing engine*, not a file manager - point a document app at it, or drive the
  > conversion/editor API directly. Big memory footprint; give it room (4-6 GB).
}
